      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T00:23:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e why not return true regardless\n`getDeclaredInstances` will have unexpected behavior in this case. We would either count the whole name as an instance, or return nothing when they don\u0027t have that format.\n\n```\nandroid.hardware.foo/bar\nandroid.hardware.foo/zed\n```\nisDeclared(\"android.hardware.foo/bar\") returns true.\ngetDeclaredInstances(\"android.hardware.foo\") returns {\"bar\", \"zed\"}.\n\n```\nblah\n```\nisDeclared(\"blah\") returns true?\ngetDeclaredInstances(\"blah\") returns {}, or {\"blah\"}?\n\nI lean more towards `{}` since it doesn\u0027t have \"/\u003cinstance\u003e\".",
      "parentUuid": "fcbf5c91_58d8a44a",
